STING IN PRD BUT MATCHED ZERO TESTS` — sibling of BE-0382's `EXISTING-TEST-SATISFIES-RUN-FILTER` but the OPPOSITE shape: the PRD's `verificationLoop.requiredBackendCommands` already contained `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...` before BE-0386 landed, BUT the `TestFakeDokploy` prefix matched ZERO existing tests anywhere in the repo (the dokployfake package's tests are TestCreateHierarchy…, TestTwoServers…, TestRequestRecordingRedactsCredentials, etc. — none start with TestFakeDokploy). The named CI/verify.sh/CONTRIBUTING gates would have silently passed against zero tests. BE-0386 adds value by (a) CREATING the canonical TestFakeDokploy* pair so the `-run` filter binds to real assertions, (b) wiring CI/verify.sh/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/AGENTS surfaces as named gates, (c) adding the static defence that pins both halves. Forward-applicable: when picking up ANY verification-suite story whose PRD `-run` filter exists, FIRST run `go test -run <Prefix> ./...` — if it shows `no tests to run` everywhere, the story MUST add canonical tests under the prefix BEFORE wiring the gates, otherwise the gates pass vacuously. (3) `CANONICAL-PAIR DUAL-INVARIANT NAMING — DETERMINISM × RECORDER-REDACTION` — TestFakeDokployContractDeterministicHierarchyIDs pins the per-server deterministic ID allocator (two independent dokployfake.New() servers driven through the same org/project/env/app/deployment chain mint byte-identical org_1/proj_1/env_1/app_1/dep_1, with per-server request counts isolated to 5/5); TestFakeDokployContractRecordedRequestsRedactCredentials pins the recorder hot path that swaps the Authorization header for output.Sentinel AND scans the body for the bearer literal (3 recorded requests across happy-path create / GET read-back / failure-path POST whose body deliberately echoes the bearer — each MUST have AuthHeader==Sentinel, Headers[Authorization]==Sentinel, no body retains the bearer literal). The SECURITY.md substring set MUST include `dokployfake.New` (constructor — deletion breaks every worker test), `Server.Requests` (recorder seam), `output.Sentinel` (the redaction substitute — a different sentinel would silently fork the redaction contract), AND `TestLiveDokploySmoke` (the AC2 opt-in-external escape hatch's test name) so auditors verify the contract from documentation alone. Substring count raised to 15 (vs BE-0385's 13). (4) `VERIFY.SH RENUMBER OF OPTIONALS BLOCK — SEVEN INSERTIONS NOW (#6→#12)` — inserting required step #12 between #11 (job worker lease) and the optionals renumbered 12→13/13→14/14→15/15→16 in the same edit (govulncheck/staticcheck/golangci-lint/goreleaser). Now SEVEN consecutive required-step insertions with optional renumbering; the next contributor adding required step #13 (BE-0387 redaction tests, canonical `go test -run TestRedaction ./...` if PRD names that filter) should follow the same edit shape AND prepare for an optional-band renumber. Per-story knobs for siblings: same as BE-0385's bullet — (a) canonical command from PRD, (b) dedicated CI step name, (c) verify.sh numeric prefix (next number after last required step; renumber trailing optionals in same edit), (d) SECURITY.md section heading and 13-15-entry substring set (per-suite invariants — preserve closed-set discipline), (e) AGENTS.md subsection mirroring SECURITY.md but speaking to maintainers (which seam each canonical-pair function pins). Load-bearing invariant unchanged: ONE FILE, SIX SURFACES, SELF-CHECK; drift on any surface fails ONE test, not six.
