ossTenant for everything else). The two matrices are STRUCTURALLY IDENTICAL (same role × action cross-product, same engine, same fixtures) but differ in resource scope (resourceIn(orgA) vs resourceIn(orgB)) and in the expected-verdict switch. Forward-applicable to ANY future security-verification story whose invariant has a "happy path × foreign-scope path" dual: BE-0398 (tenant isolation), BE-0404 (break-glass), BE-0407 (service desired-state goldens). The cross-tenant variant's switch MUST encode the engine's exact cross-tenant clause — guessing it from intuition (e.g. assuming Support is always allowed cross-tenant) fails the matrix because the engine ALSO checks the required cap via `roleCaps.has(CapSupport) && (required == CapRead || required == CapSupport)`. Verify by tracing engine.Decide BEFORE writing the test's expected-verdict switch. (3) `EXISTING-TEST-SATISFIES-RUN-FILTER` — unlike BE-0382 where the `-run TestOpenAPI` filter previously matched zero tests (the existing openapi tests were `TestBuild…` / `TestOperation…`), BE-0383's `-run TestPolicyMatrix` filter ALREADY matched the existing `TestPolicyMatrix` function in internal/controlplane/policy/policy_test.go. The story still adds value by (a) wiring the dedicated CI/verify.sh/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY surfaces (the gate did not exist as a named gate before), (b) enriching the canonical test set with the cross-tenant matrix twin so the canonical-funcs pair is load-bearing, and (c) pinning the existence of both via the static test. Per-story knobs for siblings: (a) canonical command (BE-0383 uses `go test -run TestPolicyMatrix ./...` filter-narrowed; BE-0384 will use `go test -run TestQuotaConcurrency ./...`), (b) dedicated CI step name (BE-0383: "Policy matrix tests"), (c) verify.sh numeric prefix (BE-0383 inserted `# 9. Required: policy matrix tests` between BE-0382's `# 8` and the previous `# 9. Optional: govulncheck`, renumbering optionals 9→10/10→11/11→12/12→13 in the same edit — established by BE-0380's renumber pattern), (d) SECURITY.md section heading and 13-entry substring set covering scope (internal/controlplane/policy) / determinism (deterministic fixtures) / actionable-failures (ReasonDeniedCrossTenant) / exceptions (CapSelf, CapSupport) / opt-in-external (YALLA_EXTERNAL_DOKPLOY) / envelope-pinning (yalla.output.v1, yalla.error.v1) / matrix-pair (TestPolicyMatrix, TestPolicyMatrixDeniesCrossTenant) / redaction (redacted) / CI-cadence (Every push and PR) / self-locating gate filename (verification_suite_policy_matrix_static_test.go), (e) PRD requiredBackendCommands entry already present unchanged (BE-0383 did NOT add — the existing entry satisfies the matcher), (f) canonical reference test file path + matrix-pair func-name set + the `-run` filter prefix the canonical-funcs entries MUST satisfy. Load-bearing invariant: ONE FILE, SIX SURFACES, SELF-CHECK; drift on any surface fails ONE test, not six.
