ralph/prd.json:11705:      "notes": "Implemented migration 0051_usage_events_metering_contract extending usage_events with resource scope columns, quantity, unit, source, idempotency_key, period_start/end, tenant-safe composite FKs, idempotency uniqueness, and an append-only update rejection trigger. Added UsageEventRepository.Append with validation, tenant-scope existence checks, metadata redaction, active subscription period assignment with UTC calendar fallback, replay-safe duplicate idempotency handling, and adjustment event support. Added isolated Postgres tests for idempotency, redaction, correction events, period assignment, validation failure, tenant-scope not-found, and database append-only behavior. No public HTTP surface was added in this persistence story, so yalla.output.v1/yalla.error.v1 route envelope criteria are not applicable until a usage-events API lands."
ralph/prd.json:11710:      "description": "Aggregate usage_events and metric samples into billing-period counters.",
ralph/prd.json:11724:      "notes": "Implemented migration 0052_usage_counters with usage_counters and usage_counter_adjustments. Added UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents to replay append-only usage_events into deterministic org-scoped counters keyed by resource/unit/source/period/version, upsert open periods idempotently, freeze previously closed counters, and append only net-new late-event adjustments. Added integration coverage for replay idempotency, closed-period late adjustments, validation, tenant not-found, rollback on partial failure, and concurrent aggregators. No public HTTP surface was added in this persistence story, so yalla.output.v1/yalla.error.v1 route envelope criteria are not applicable until a usage-counters API or export endpoint consumes this repository."
ralph/prd.json:11819:      "notes": "Completed container resource metering with billing-grade container_cpu_millicore_seconds and container_memory_mb_hours definitions/resources, Dokploy monitoring sample normalization, cAdvisor/Docker-style runtime stats collection with counter-reset handling, dokploy_refs-backed service attribution with ambiguous/deleted-service quarantine, idempotent usage_events emission, aggregation into usage_counters, tenant-isolation coverage, and redaction-safe metadata. No public HTTP surface was added in this metering-source story, so JSON envelope route criteria remain not applicable until an API consumes the metering output."
ralph/prd.json:11933:      "notes": "Implemented metering UsageReconciler over append-only usage_events and usage_counters. The worker service validates tenant/period input, replays counters idempotently through UsageCounterRepository, detects metric gaps, overlapping duplicate windows, counter resets, and quarantined samples, and records low-confidence discrepancies as drift findings with request/correlation ids. Tests cover open-period replay repair, closed-period late adjustments without double-counting, gap/quarantine findings, duplicate-window/counter-reset detection, validation, and tenant-scoped not-found behavior."
