 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Soft/non-billing tracked metrics that must be customer-visible still flow through durable `usage_events` and `usage_counters`: `MetricDefinition.BillingGrade=false` controls billing semantics, not persistence; add a `quota_resource` constant/domain value when the metric must appear in usage APIs or billing export snapshots.
 - Invoice-period close snapshots compose existing billing surfaces instead of duplicating them: freeze `usage_counters` plus summed `usage_counter_adjustments` into `invoice_snapshot_items`, link the provider-neutral `billing_exports` row for export status/readback, store plan version + entitlement revision + source checksums for reproducibility, and handle corrections by marking the old snapshot `reopened` with an audit event before creating the next `close_version`.
 - Usage reconciliation lives at the metering boundary: inspect append-only `usage_events` window metadata, replay counters through `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents`, rely on `usage_counter_adjustments` for closed-period late usage idempotency, and record low-confidence gaps/quarantines/resets as value-free operator drift findings until a dedicated usage-drift taxonomy exists.
 - Metered overage hooks run at the usage-counter aggregation boundary, not inside quota/resource mutation code: runtime entitlement resolution carries plan/subscription metadata, `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents` stamps `usage_counters` with `entitlement_key`, `overage_policy_mode`, `overage_decision`, included/overage quantities, and an audit event, and `BillingExportRepository.Prepare` snapshots those fields into `billing_export_items` so provider adapters can bill/review overages without changing quota code.
