is test. (2) The support cross-tenant exception is suppressed on the wire by construction — environmentIDResolver pins OrganizationID to principal.home — so the support cross-tenant ALLOW only fires at the engine layer against a hand-built foreign-org Resource. The wire-level "wrong organization" probe surfaces as 404 E_NOT_FOUND from the tenant-scoped GetByID query (never 403, which would confirm existence), and the body must not echo the foreign org id. The contract-test helper bakes in a single canonical principal (getEnvironmentHandlerFor takes `t, reader` only, with authForEnvGet's hardcoded principal), so this matrix introduces a per-test identity-injected helper LOCAL to the policy file (getEnvironmentByIDHandlerForIdentity, signature `(id auth.Identity, authErr error, reader EnvironmentReader) http.Handler`) modelled on listProjectsHandlerFor / listProjectEnvironmentsHandlerFor — adding the helper locally avoids modifying the 9 contract tests that already use the simpler form. ACTION-CONSTANT gotcha to pin: routes.go:574 sets `RequiredAction: string(policy.ActionEnvironmentRead)` for this route, NOT `policy.ActionEnvRead` — both are CapRead per catalog.go but they're different catalog entries (env-vars vs env entity); mixing them up silently swaps which catalog row a future tier-upgrade watches. Forward-applicable to every future bare-id matrix on a deep resource (service.read on /v1/services/{service_id}, deployment.read on /v1/deployments/{deployment_id}, etc).
